    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d231-a1">

                <pb facs="0503" n="483" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg483"/>

                <head>Mr. Chase to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Department</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 11, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to return herewith the
                    despatch of Lord Lyons, of the 22d ultimo, and accompanying papers, relative to
                    the voyage of the British bark Julia from Amoy.</p>
                <p>The charter-party is express in its provisions that the “charterers (are) to have
                    the option of sending the vessel to Montreal, New York, Charleston, or New
                    Orleans, but to one port only, and to either of the southern ports only, if the
                    blockade is raised and the port open for commerce,” of which the master would be
                    advised on reaching St. Thomas.</p>
                <p>Relying on the integrity of the papers submitted, I am satisfied that the voyage
                    to be made is perfectly legitimate, and that the insertion of the name of
                    Charleston in a charter-party made in China, with the provision above cited, is
                    no cause for seizure on the arrival of this bark into the port of New York, and
                    have so advised the collector of customs of that port.</p>
                <p>With great respect,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. P. CHASE, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Treasur</hi>y.
                    </signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
